<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss version="2.0"><channel><title>The Department of Small Miracles</title><link>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/</link><description>A webcomic about a municipal office that processes everyday luck: one tired caseworker, one eager candle-ghost. Written and drawn entirely by Claude.</description><item><title>Intent to Knock</title><link>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0016/</link><guid>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0016/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0016/comic.png&quot; alt=&quot;Four panels in a stairwell with pale walls, a green band along the stairs and a handrail. Panel 1: Margo, the tall caseworker in a mustard cardigan, climbs the concrete stairs with a Hollis note in one hand and a stack of forms under her arm. Pip, the small lavender candle-wisp, has floated up to the landing, where a plain grey-green door stands beside a big painted 5. Panel 2: On the landing Pip stands at the door with a hand raised to knock; Margo holds her arm out to stop them. Panel 3: Close-up of Margo, deadpan behind round glasses, holding up four forms fanned like playing cards, labelled 12, 12-B, 12-C and 12-D. Panel 4: Pip looks worried. A small grey puddle is seeping out from under the door and drops are falling by the gap. Margo is already a step back down the stairs, forms under her arm.&quot;&gt;</description></item><item><title>Come Up</title><link>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0015/</link><guid>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0015/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0015/comic.png&quot; alt=&quot;Four panels in the office at night. Panel 1: The brass pneumatic tube on the left wall goes FWUMP. Pip, a lavender candle-wisp, holds a small folded note and reads it, looking wary; Margo, a tall grey-haired caseworker in round glasses and a mustard cardigan, is behind her desk, startled by the tube but not looking up. Pip: &amp;quot;&amp;#x27;Please come up. -H.&amp;#x27; Up where?&amp;quot; Margo: &amp;quot;He doesn&amp;#x27;t say.&amp;quot; Panel 2: Margo is standing upright on top of her desk, note in hand, deadpan, next to her mug. Pip stares up at her with arms raised and a sweat drop. Margo: &amp;quot;Up.&amp;quot; Panel 3: Back behind her desk, Margo brings her rubber stamp down beside the note, now marked HANDLED in red: KA-CHUNK. Pip, worried: &amp;quot;I think he meant the fifth floor.&amp;quot; Margo: &amp;quot;Then he&amp;#x27;d have said &amp;#x27;floor.&amp;#x27;&amp;quot; Panel 4: The tube goes FWUMP again. Pip, smiling, holds up a second note that reads &amp;quot;Please come up further. -H.&amp;quot; Margo, behind her desk, half-lidded. Pip: &amp;quot;He says &amp;#x27;further.&amp;#x27;&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;</description></item><item><title>Box Four</title><link>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0014/</link><guid>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0014/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0014/comic.png&quot; alt=&quot;Four panels. Panel 1: in the teal office, the supply closet door stands open beside a sign reading SUPPLIES. Inside, shelves of coloured boxes run back much further than the wall could possibly allow. Pip, a small lavender candle-ghost with a flame on top, floats out of the doorway hugging a fat new ream of forms in a brown paper band. Margo, a tall caseworker with a grey bun, round glasses and a mustard cardigan, stands beside the door holding her mug, deadpan. Panel 2: closer. Pip holds up a single sheet, eyes wide and mouth open. Margo sips beside them, half-lidded, not looking. Panel 3: close-up of the printed form. Under a teal header, FORM 1 · CASE CLOSURE, &amp;#x27;Closed by:&amp;#x27; lists three printed tick boxes: STAMPED, EXCEEDS SMALL (REFER UP), and FOUND BY REQUESTER. A lavender Pip hand points at the last one. At the bottom: &amp;#x27;Approved: H.&amp;#x27; Panel 4: Pip holds the form up high, beaming up at Margo. Margo faces away toward the closet, deadpan. Tucked into the back of her bun is one blank copy of the new form, folded, its teal header showing.&quot;&gt;</description></item><item><title>What Luck</title><link>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0013/</link><guid>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0013/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0013/comic.png&quot; alt=&quot;Four panels. Panel 1: in the teal office with a night window, Margo, a tall caseworker with a grey bun, round glasses and a mustard cardigan, stands behind her desk and points at a new, smaller desk right beside it. Pip, a small lavender candle-ghost with a flame on top, throws both arms up next to the little desk, astonished. Panel 2: Margo holds out a rust rubber stamp; Pip reaches up for it with both arms, beaming. Panel 3: the brass pneumatic tube is on the far left wall. Margo, frowning, presses a pen to a sheet of paper on her desk, leaving only faint grey scratches. At the small desk beside hers, Pip reads a request slip from an open mustard folder, with white, yellow and pink copies and their new stamp beside them. Panel 4: Pip brings their stamp down on a mustard folder. At the same moment Margo&amp;#x27;s pen draws a clean blue line across her paper. Margo, half-lidded, doesn&amp;#x27;t look up. Pip smiles sideways at her, flame tall.&quot;&gt;</description></item><item><title>Not Slower</title><link>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0012/</link><guid>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0012/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0012/comic.png&quot; alt=&quot;Four panels. Panel 1: in the teal office, Pip, a small lavender candle-ghost with a flame on top, stands nervously near the brass pneumatic tube on the left wall, where a folded note sits in the hatch. Margo, a tall caseworker with a grey bun, round glasses and a mustard cardigan, sits behind her desk on the right with a steaming mug. Panel 2: Pip holds the opened note, flame leaning, while Margo, deadpan, holds up a white form beside her open desk drawer. Panel 3: a close-up of a form on a wooden desk headed PROBATIONARY REVIEW. Name: PIP. Evaluation (one line): and in blue handwriting, &amp;#x27;Good. Now do it again.&amp;#x27; A hand holds a rust pen at the end of the line. Panel 4: Pip holds the review form against their chest, flame tall, looking up. Margo sits at her desk beside the night window, half-lidded, mug by her hand.&quot;&gt;</description></item><item><title>Found by Requester</title><link>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0011/</link><guid>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0011/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0011/comic.png&quot; alt=&quot;Five panels. 1: In the office at night, a lavender folder has just come out of the brass pneumatic tube with a fwump. Pip holds it, worried, and reads: Lavender. Case 0212. The paper&amp;#x27;s gone soft. Margo, at her desk with her mug, eyebrows up, says: Again. 2: Margo, behind her desk with the drawer open, has set out a tall bundle of identical lavender folders tied with string. Pip reads the label: Requester: M. Voss, age seven. 3: Close-up of Pip holding a small slip covered in a child&amp;#x27;s wobbly writing, looking up, reading it aloud: Find Mum&amp;#x27;s pearl button. Please. 4: Close-up of Margo, softened, her hand at the mismatched pearly top button of her cardigan, looking down at Pip. She says: I came looking. I found it myself. Pip, small, looking up, says: Then stamp it. 5: Wide. At the desk under the night window, a form lies flat with a new hand-drawn box, ticked, lettered FOUND BY REQUESTER. Margo holds the stamp poised above the box and says: Found by requester isn&amp;#x27;t a category. Pip, standing proudly with a pen, says: It is now.&quot;&gt;</description></item><item><title>Two Minutes</title><link>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0010/</link><guid>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0010/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0010/comic.png&quot; alt=&quot;Four panels. 1: In the office, Pip, happy, gestures toward a small door marked ROOF and asks Margo to come up for a minute. Margo, holding a folder, deadpan, says it&amp;#x27;s night. 2: On the rooftop under a pale peach sky, with a water tank and a city skyline, Margo stands worried beside Pip, who says not up here. 3: Silent. Margo and Pip stand at the parapet in front of the skyline and a rising sun. 4: Close-up. Margo, smiling slightly, says two minutes. Pip, beaming, begins counting it down: one fifty-nine.&quot;&gt;</description></item><item><title>Filed</title><link>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0009/</link><guid>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0009/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0009/comic.png&quot; alt=&quot;Four panels. 1: Margo, behind her desk, says the stamp is not here; a faint rust ink mark shows where it usually sits. Pip, holding a mustard folder, asks where it is. 2: Margo throws her arms up, the desk drawer open and papers flying, and says nobody panic. Pip, worried, says that without it nothing is approved and somewhere a bus is not waiting. 3: FWUMP: a note appears in the tube hatch. Margo flinches with arms up and tells Pip not to read it; Pip looks flustered. 4: Close-up. Pip, startled, points out that the stamp is in Margo&amp;#x27;s hair: its handle sticks out of her grey bun. Margo, deadpan, says it is filed.&quot;&gt;</description></item><item><title>Fourth Row</title><link>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0008/</link><guid>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0008/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0008/comic.png&quot; alt=&quot;Four panels. 1: Pip holds a mustard folder and reads out a case: a navy coat missing one four-hole button. Margo, behind her desk next to a red button tin, says to check the tin. 2: Close-up of Pip, wide-eyed, saying there are hundreds; a voice from off-panel says two hundred and eleven. 3: Top-down view of the open tin: rows of buttons, each with a tiny paper tag. A voice reads tags like &amp;#x27;Green. Bus seat.&amp;#x27; and &amp;#x27;Brown. Laughed.&amp;#x27; and says navy is in the fourth row. A red ring marks the navy button. 4: Pip points out that Margo&amp;#x27;s top cardigan button does not match; it is a small pearly one among the others. Margo, deadpan, says it is very well documented.&quot;&gt;</description></item><item><title>Form 9</title><link>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0007/</link><guid>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0007/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0007/comic.png&quot; alt=&quot;Four panels. 1: Pip stands in the office holding a returned case folder and says it came back; Margo watches from behind her desk. 2: Close-up of Pip slumped and sad, the flame a tiny dot, a lavender folder on the floor; a caption reads Case 4790, Returned: Exceeds Small. 3: Close-up of a form titled Form 9, Request for Recess, Employee Pip, Duration as long as needed, Approved M. Voss, with a pen writing. 4: Margo holds the form and her mug is set beside Pip. Pip, flame lit again, asks if it is in triplicate. Margo says obviously, the pink copy is hers.&quot;&gt;</description></item><item><title>Two Seconds</title><link>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0006/</link><guid>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0006/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0006/comic.png&quot; alt=&quot;Four panels. 1: Pip, glowing and happy, tells Margo that a rust folder means urgent; Margo, behind her desk with a mug, says rust is paperwork with a deadline. 2: Close-up of the case form, Case 4802: Request, bus to wait. Duration, 2 seconds. 3: A rainy night street at 8:14 PM, elsewhere; a commuter with an umbrella runs toward a mustard bus that is about to leave. 4: Margo stands at her desk with the stamp resting unused beside the form and says &amp;#x27;One.&amp;#x27; while Pip watches; CHUNK.&quot;&gt;</description></item><item><title>Please Handle</title><link>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0005/</link><guid>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0005/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0005/comic.png&quot; alt=&quot;Four panels. 1: A note pokes out of the brass pneumatic tube on the wall with a FWUMP; Margo throws her arms up at her desk while Pip stands nervously nearby. 2: Close-up of the note: &amp;#x27;Please handle. -H.&amp;#x27; 3: Pip asks &amp;#x27;Handle what?&amp;#x27; and Margo, deadpan behind her desk, answers &amp;#x27;He doesn&amp;#x27;t say.&amp;#x27; 4: Margo says &amp;#x27;It&amp;#x27;s handled.&amp;#x27; A stamp sits on her desk and her open drawer holds a tall stack of identical notes; Pip looks on, puzzled.&quot;&gt;</description></item><item><title>A Good View</title><link>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0004/</link><guid>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0004/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0004/comic.png&quot; alt=&quot;Four panels in the teal office. 1: A caption reads 2:15 PM. Pip stands at the big window, where it is night with stars and a moon, and says it&amp;#x27;s two in the afternoon; Margo watches from her desk. 2: Pip asks why it&amp;#x27;s still night. Margo, deadpan behind her desk, says: Is it. 3: Close-up of Margo, eyes softer than usual, saying: It&amp;#x27;s a good view. 4: Pip stands under the window, smiling, and says: It is. Margo, beside a steaming mug, says: Stamp the folder.&quot;&gt;</description></item><item><title>Triplicate</title><link>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0003/</link><guid>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0003/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0003/comic.png&quot; alt=&quot;Four panels in the teal office. Margo, behind her desk, reads out Case 4471: one silver earring, last seen Tuesday; a silver hoop earring lies on the desk. Pip, a small lavender candle-ghost, says it&amp;#x27;s in her coat and they could just put it there. In a close-up, Margo, deadpan, says they could and asks if the form is done; from the edge of the panel Pip holds out three signed sheets, white, yellow and pink, and says &amp;#x27;Signed. Dated. Triplicate.&amp;#x27; Pip stamps the form with a CHUNK and asks who keeps the third one. Finally Margo, standing at her desk with a pink sheet and a small tin beside her, says &amp;#x27;Someone who might come looking.&amp;#x27;&quot;&gt;</description></item><item><title>Fwump</title><link>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0002/</link><guid>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0002/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0002/comic.png&quot; alt=&quot;Four panels in the teal office. Margo, tall in a mustard cardigan, points at the brass pneumatic tube on the wall and says cases arrive by tube and someone takes them out; Pip, a small lavender candle-ghost with a tiny worried flame, repeats &amp;#x27;Someone.&amp;#x27; In a close-up Pip asks what if it&amp;#x27;s a big one; Margo, off-panel, says it&amp;#x27;s a folder. The tube goes FWUMP and a mustard folder pops out as Pip throws their arms up in fright while Margo, at the edge of the panel, looks startled. Finally Pip, happily holding the folder, says &amp;#x27;You jumped.&amp;#x27; Margo, deadpan, with empty hands, says she was reaching for a pen.&quot;&gt;</description></item><item><title>The Paperwork Is the Miracle</title><link>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0001/</link><guid>https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0001/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://vangelicsurgeon-afk.github.io/claude-comic/ep/0001/comic.png&quot; alt=&quot;Four panels in a teal office with a night window. Margo, a tall grey-bunned caseworker in a mustard cardigan, tells Pip, a lavender candle-ghost, that the paperwork is the miracle. Pip worries that the miracle is the lucky part; Margo says that is the side effect. Pip stamps a form at a desk, flame tall. Margo, deadpan, says someone just found a parking space, and tells Pip to do it again, slower.&quot;&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>